# Internal helper -- NOT meant to be run standalone via IC.
# PCALLed by VVDN_35L35R_COORDINATED_OPS.scn when VDN602
# touches down (ATALT 0 trigger) + a 30.0s delay -- the combined
# gap to this file's own first MOVE command (0.00s, real
# constant-acceleration ground roll from the lineup point to VR at the
# 1.2NM-from-threshold liftoff point, see this scenario's own header)
# gives a total observable touchdown -> visible-roll-start gap of
# 30.00s, matching the explicit ~30s
# request. VDN702 is a real A333, VR=134.4kt (BADA Vstall_TO x 1.2).
# Takeoff-roll -> climb -> real SID VIDEN 2G portion, timestamps re-based
# so 00:00:00.00 = the moment this file is PCALLed.
# Also embeds, at t=00:00:00.00 (the instant VDN702 itself visibly
# starts rolling), a PCALL clearing VDN703 onto RWY 35R from its
# pre-crossing taxiway hold (see _INTERNAL_ENTER_RWY_*.scn).
# Also embeds, at t=00:02:23.00, a PCALL resuming the SAME-
# numbered held arrival via _INTERNAL_ARR_RESUME_VDN602. This time is
# MAX(far-end-crossing time [77.39s, +3s margin past this
# departure's own computed closest approach to the real RWY 35R far-end
# reference point 16.0574,108.1984], arrival's-own-safe-minimum
# [143.00s -- estimated real touchdown-to-hold-point-reached time
# for the paired arrival, +40s margin]) -- NOT just the far-end time alone,
# which was found live-tested to be a real safety bug: the arrival could
# get forcibly resumed (teleported via MOVE) onto RWY 35R before it had
# actually finished taxiing to its hold point.

00:00:00.00>MOVE VDN702,16.029700,108.202400,0,352,4.0
00:00:00.00>PCALL _INTERNAL_ENTER_RWY_VDN703
